cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Shared readouts, not S³: what drives forgetting in a toy quaternion network"
abstract: >-
  A controlled study of catastrophic forgetting in small quaternion networks.
  Forgetting comes mostly from reading two tasks out of one shared output
  quaternion, and the remaining gap between unit-quaternion (S³) and free
  weights comes from the amplitude × unit-quaternion factorization shrinking
  direction updates by A², not from the sphere itself. With both fixed, the
  quaternion network matches real-valued MLPs. Includes a reproducible
  JavaScript engine, raw results and an interactive browser workbench.
